The earlier factorization was wrong. Setting up: n(n−1)/2 = n + 170 → n² − 3n − 340 = 0. The factors should be (n − 20)(n + 17) = 0, since 20 × 17 = 340 and 20 − 17 = 3. So n = 20, not 17.

Verification: C(20,2) = 190, and subsets with at most one element = 1 + 20 = 21. Indeed 190 − 21 = 169. ✓

